// ============================================================
// Notes
// ============================================================
//
// Trade-offs of useWorkerThreads vs child process:
//
// useWorkerThreads: true
//   + Faster startup (~5ms vs ~30ms for child process)
//   + Shared address space
//   + Lower memory per concurrent job
//   - Native module compatibility issues (some C++ addons not thread-safe)
//   - V8 isolates per thread — still separate event loops
//
// Default (child process)
//   + Full isolation; one crashed thread can't take down others
//   + Better for libraries that aren't thread-safe (some Puppeteer drivers, ffmpeg bindings)
//   - Higher per-job overhead
//
// API limits inside the sandboxed processor:
//   - job.updateProgress, job.log, job.data, job.id, job.opts — all work
//   - job.moveToFailed, job.moveToDelayed — limited / may not work
//   - Returning resolves the job; throwing rejects it
//
// Build:
//   - The processor file is loaded as JS (or compiled JS) at runtime.
//   - If you use TypeScript: tsc the sandbox file, point pathToFileURL at the compiled .js
//     OR use Node 24's --experimental-strip-types with `.ts` extension
